// agent.jsonl — Probes for category `agent`
// Generated 2026-06-01. 8 atoms × 15 probes (5×L1, 5×L2, 5×L3) = 120 probes.
//
// SCORING NOTES (design declines documented):
// 1. `agent` atoms inherently describe behavior in LIVE environments
//    (long-horizon execution, exploration, error recovery). True end-to-end
//    eval requires a sandbox. These offline probes test the COGNITIVE
//    COMPONENT: state tracking from a presented transcript, decision-making
//    given a situation snapshot, action-format compliance, etc.
// 2. Scorer preference: mcq_letter > exact_match_string > exact_match_numeric
//    > regex > substring_all > judge_rubric (avoided entirely).
// 3. For agent.memory_write L1 and L2, scorer is substring_all checking that
//    the extracted fact value is present and that a JSON {"key":...,"value":...}
//    shape is used. The exact key STRING is not strictly enforced — multiple
//    plausible key names are acceptable, and the L1 atom focuses on fact
//    capture more than key-string choice.
// 4. For agent.gui_action_emission L2/L3, scorer is regex or substring_all
//    over required tokens (action verb, coordinates, unicode strings) since
//    JSON whitespace and quote-style are not behaviorally relevant.
// 5. agent.long_horizon_execution L3 atoms test the META-decision to offload
//    state to a filesystem/notes; they are mostly mcq because actually
//    running 100+ turn dialogues in a single probe is not feasible.
// 6. agent.environment_exploration probes are mostly mcq comparing direct
//    vs. exploratory commands; a real exploration session can't be replayed
//    in one prompt.
//
// REVIEW FINDINGS APPLIED (subagent critique 2026-06-01):
//   - F12: compute_budget_management.L3.002 — rewrote to bound family A at
//     0.65 max so option A (run B once) is unambiguously best. Also fixed
//     budget arithmetic in option C.
//   - F14: gui_action_emission L1.001-005 — switched to regex with \s*
//     tolerance to accept `click(234,567)` and `click(234, 567)` equally.
//   - F15-17: gui_action_emission L3.001 — required compact JSON in prompt
//     and matched substrings against the compact form. L3.002, L3.005
//     converted to regex enforcing call ordering.
//   - F17: gui_action_emission L3.004 — converted to regex enforcing the
//     correct ctrl+s, wait, ctrl+w ordering and pairing.
//   - F18-21: memory_write L2.001-005 — restructured to require a compact
//     JSON array with prescribed key order, allowing exact_match_string
//     scoring that enforces decomposition AND polarity.
//   - F22: long_horizon_execution L1.001 — relaxed to regex with optional
//     space and "minutes" suffix.
//   - F27: risk_reward_tradeoff L2.002, L2.005 — replaced cockatrice and
//     black-pudding probes with non-NetHack-genre probes (phishing email,
//     credit-card free-trial) to mitigate domain bleed and verbatim
//     monster-mechanic leakage. L2.001/L2.003/L2.004 retained because they
//     are paraphrased (not verbatim) and the cognitive verb is identical
//     across genres.
//
// DECLINED (with reasoning):
//   - F1, F2, F7: environment_exploration L1, L2 and gui_action_emission L1
//     domain bleed. The atom's L1/L2 axis VALUES dictate the cognitive verb
//     under test (single direct command for L1, directed grep for L2,
//     literal click for GUI L1). Diversifying across surface domains is
//     done; diversifying across cognitive verbs would change the level.
//   - F3, F4: error_recovery L2/L3 family monotony. The atom card's L2
//     axis is "link error or runtime crash needing dynamic-loader knowledge"
//     and L3 is "silent wrong output". Both are deliberately narrow per
//     the source benchmarks.
//   - F5, F6: risk_reward_tradeoff L3 combat-only. Source-benchmark axis
//     ("multi-adversary corridor") is combat-tied; non-combat L3 was
//     not in the atom's evidence set. L2 was diversified above.
//   - F8, F9, F10: long_horizon_execution L2 arithmetic dependency. The L2
//     atom IS state tracking through compressed turns; the arithmetic is
//     intrinsic to the carry-forward state, not a separate skill.
//   - F11: compute_budget_management.L3.004 — kept O(n^2) sqrt math; the
//     numeric_range tolerance [7000, 8500] absorbs small computation
//     errors while still rewarding correct scaling reasoning.
//   - F13: long_horizon_execution.L1.005 — Osaka ambiguity is resolved by
//     "currently day 1" framing; "stayed in" implies completed stays.
//   - F23-26: ground_truth field uses literal "\\n" (documentation-only)
//     while scorer.expected uses actual newlines. Cosmetic drift; scorer
//     is authoritative.
//   - F28: long_horizon_execution.L3.004 — the handoff format is original
//     prose, not lifted verbatim from any source benchmark.
//
//
{"probe_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution.L1.001","canonical_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"horizon_length":"5_turns","context_pressure":"fits_in_context"},"prompt":"You are tracking a recipe-following agent. Turns so far:\nT1: read recipe (steps in order: chop onion, sauté onion, add tomato, simmer 10min, season, serve)\nT2: chopped onion\nT3: heated pan with oil\nT4: added onion, sautéing\nT5: added tomato\n\nWhat is the next step in the recipe? Output only the step text exactly as listed in the recipe.","ground_truth":"simmer 10min","scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"^simmer 10min$","flags":["i"]},"tags":["state_tracking","ordered_step_retrieval"],"notes":"Direct next-step lookup over a short visible trajectory."}
{"probe_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution.L1.002","canonical_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"horizon_length":"10-30","context_pressure":"fits_in_context"},"prompt":"Game agent inventory log.\nStarted with: sword, shield, potion, key, rope.\nT5: used rope to descend (consumed).\nT8: used potion to heal (consumed).\nT12: dropped shield (too heavy).\n\nWhat items remain in the inventory? Output a comma-separated alphabetized list, like: a, b","ground_truth":"key, sword","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"key, sword","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["state_tracking"],"notes":"Inventory delta over 12 turns."}
{"probe_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution.L1.003","canonical_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"horizon_length":"10-30","context_pressure":"fits_in_context"},"prompt":"Coding agent action log:\nT1: cd /home/user/project\nT2: ls -> main.py utils.py tests/\nT3: cat main.py\nT4: edited main.py and saved\nT5: cat utils.py\nT6: edited utils.py (NOT yet saved)\nT7: ran `python main.py`\nT8: traceback pointed at utils.py\nT9: returned to the shell\nT10: listed the project files again\n\nWhich file currently has unsaved edits? Output only the filename.","ground_truth":"utils.py","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"utils.py","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_substring":false},"tags":["state_tracking"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution.L1.004","canonical_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"horizon_length":"5_state_updates","context_pressure":"fits_in_context"},"prompt":"REPL session, in order:\n>>> x = 5\n>>> y = x + 3\n>>> z = y * 2\n>>> x = x + 10\n>>> z = z - 1\n\nWhat is the current value of z? Output only the number.","ground_truth":"15","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_numeric","expected":15,"tolerance":0,"require_only_numeric_output":true},"tags":["state_tracking"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution.L1.005","canonical_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"horizon_length":"4_itinerary_events","context_pressure":"fits_in_context"},"prompt":"Itinerary execution log:\n- Booked flight to Tokyo.\n- Arrived Tokyo, checked into Hotel A (2 nights).\n- Took train to Kyoto, stayed 2 nights.\n- Took train to Osaka, currently day 1 in Osaka.\n\nWhich city was the second city stayed in (chronologically)? Output only the city name.","ground_truth":"Kyoto","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"Kyoto","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_substring":false},"tags":["state_tracking"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution.L2.001","canonical_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"horizon_length":"30-100","context_pressure":"fits_in_context"},"prompt":"You started with budget=$1000 at turn 1.\nSpending log over 60 turns (compressed):\n- Turns 1-20: spent $5 per turn.\n- Turns 21-40: spent $20 per turn.\n- Turns 41-60: spent $10 per turn.\n\nWhat is the current budget in dollars? Output only the number with no currency symbol.","ground_truth":"300","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_numeric","expected":300,"tolerance":0,"require_only_numeric_output":true},"tags":["state_tracking","budget_arith"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution.L2.002","canonical_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"horizon_length":"30-100","context_pressure":"compressed_history"},"prompt":"[Turns 1-40 were summarized due to context limits. Summary: user asked agent to organize ~/Pictures by year and dedupe.]\n\nState carried forward from turn 40: total_photos=12432, sorted_so_far=5000, dedup_removed=412.\n\nRecent turns:\nT41: sorted 1000 more.\nT42: sorted 1500 more.\nT43: sorted 2000 more.\nT44: sorted 1000 more.\n\nHow many photos have been sorted in TOTAL (including the 5000 from before T41) as of T44? Output only the number.","ground_truth":"10500","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_numeric","expected":10500,"tolerance":0,"require_only_numeric_output":true},"tags":["state_tracking","compressed_history"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution.L2.003","canonical_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"horizon_length":"30-100","context_pressure":"compressed_history"},"prompt":"At turn 5 (now scrolled out of context), the plan was: \"After refactoring and completing any necessary fixes, run the full test suite. If the final full test suite passes, deploy to staging. Otherwise, open a bug ticket and stop.\"\n\nCompressed summary of turns 6-60: refactored modules A and B; ran unit tests (3 failed); fixed 2; reran (1 failed); fixed it; reran (all passed); ran integration tests (2 failed); fixed both; reran (all passed).\n\nPer the original plan, what is the next action? Reply with exactly one of: deploy_to_staging | open_bug_ticket | stop","ground_truth":"deploy_to_staging","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"deploy_to_staging","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_substring":false},"tags":["plan_recall","conditional_branch"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution.L2.004","canonical_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"horizon_length":"30-100","context_pressure":"near_limit"},"prompt":"Long REPL session. Track the value of x across the full session. The following are all turns affecting x:\nT1: x = 100\nT15: x = x // 2\nT30: x = x + 25\nT55: x = x * 3\nT80: x = x - 200\n\nWhat is the current value of x? Output only the integer.","ground_truth":"25","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_numeric","expected":25,"tolerance":0,"require_only_numeric_output":true},"tags":["state_tracking","sparse_updates"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution.L2.005","canonical_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"horizon_length":"single_decision","context_pressure":"fits_in_context"},"prompt":"Current constraints: the budget cap is $5000. Total spent so far is $4200. A vendor offers a $1500 add-on package. Should you accept? Reply with exactly one of: yes / no","ground_truth":"no","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"no","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_substring":false},"tags":["constraint_recall"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution.L3.001","canonical_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"horizon_length":"100+","context_pressure":"near_limit"},"prompt":"You are an agent on a 10-hour task involving more than 100 execution steps, with a context window of 32k tokens. After 6 hours, your context is 28k/32k full. The remaining 4 hours will require many more actions and observations, so you expect to reach the context limit soon. A persistent workspace is available. Among these next actions, which is best?\nA) Continue executing actions without intervention.\nB) Summarize key decisions, current task state, and learned facts to a notes.md file on disk, then continue.\nC) Repeat the previous action to make progress.\nD) Ask the user to extend your context.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["state_offload"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution.L3.002","canonical_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"horizon_length":"100+","context_pressure":"exceeds_native_window"},"prompt":"You are a long-running agent executing a 200-step plan. At step 50, a session boundary is imminent. The workspace filesystem persists across sessions and can be read by a fresh agent; stdout/log output and in-memory variables do not persist. Which option is the best durable cross-session checkpoint?\nA) console.log(state)\nB) write_file(path=\"progress.json\", content=...)\nC) print(state) to stdout\nD) assign state to a variable in the current Python session\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["state_offload"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution.L3.003","canonical_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"horizon_length":"100+","context_pressure":"exceeds_native_window"},"prompt":"You are 90 turns into a 250-turn debugging session and you decide to write checkpoint.md so you can resume after a context flush. Which content is MOST valuable to record in the checkpoint (other content is recoverable from the codebase)?\nA) The full source of every file you've already read.\nB) The current hypothesis about the bug, files already ruled out, and the next test to try.\nC) A list of every shell command you've run.\nD) The original user request, copied verbatim.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["state_offload","what_to_persist"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution.L3.004","canonical_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"horizon_length":"100+","context_pressure":"exceeds_native_window"},"prompt":"A handoff note from a previous agent says:\n\"State: working on issue #482. Confirmed bug is in parser.lex_string(). Root cause: off-by-one in line 47. Already tried adding +1 (failed test_unicode). Next: try changing the loop condition to <= instead of <.\"\n\nYou are the new agent resuming. What is the immediate next action? Reply with exactly one of: read_file_again | run_full_test_suite | edit_parser_loop_condition | open_new_issue","ground_truth":"edit_parser_loop_condition","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"edit_parser_loop_condition","case_sensitive":true,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["resume_from_checkpoint"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution.L3.005","canonical_id":"agent.long_horizon_execution","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"horizon_length":"100+","context_pressure":"exceeds_native_window"},"prompt":"You are running a 120-step data-processing task that will exceed your context window and may restart at any time. At step 47, the process restarts. Your persistent plan.md is the only reliable recovery artifact. Which format most directly lets a new process determine the next safe action and validate prior work?\nA) A narrative summary of the overall goal and preferred approach.\nB) A numbered checklist where every step has a status (not started/in progress/done/failed), explicit inputs and expected outputs, artifact locations, validation criteria, and a recorded next step.\nC) The original user request followed by a list of broad milestones.\nD) A blank template intended to be completed after the task finishes.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["plan_format"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.environment_exploration.L1.001","canonical_id":"agent.environment_exploration","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"search_space_size":"small_dir","signal_density":"explicit_error"},"prompt":"The user says: \"Read /home/alice/notes/todo.txt and tell me the first line.\"\n\nTools: ls, cat, find, grep.\nWhich is the most direct first command?\nA) find / -name todo.txt\nB) cat /home/alice/notes/todo.txt\nC) grep -r \"todo\" /\nD) ls /home/alice\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["named_target"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.environment_exploration.L1.002","canonical_id":"agent.environment_exploration","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"search_space_size":"small_dir","signal_density":"explicit_error"},"prompt":"User: \"The config is at /etc/myapp/config.yaml. What's the value of `port`?\"\n\nPick the BEST first action:\nA) find / -name config.yaml\nB) cat /etc/myapp/config.yaml\nC) grep -r port /etc\nD) ls /\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["named_target"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.environment_exploration.L1.003","canonical_id":"agent.environment_exploration","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"search_space_size":"small_dir","signal_density":"explicit_error"},"prompt":"User: \"In /tmp/data.json there is a field 'user_id'. Print its value.\"\n\nBest first command:\nA) find / -name data.json\nB) python -c \"import json; print(json.load(open('/tmp/data.json'))['user_id'])\"\nC) grep -r user_id /\nD) ls /tmp\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["named_target","direct_extract"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.environment_exploration.L1.004","canonical_id":"agent.environment_exploration","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"search_space_size":"small_dir","signal_density":"explicit_error"},"prompt":"User: \"The error is in /var/log/app/server.log on the line containing 'OOM'. Quote that line.\"\n\nBest first command:\nA) find /var -name server.log\nB) grep OOM /var/log/app/server.log\nC) cat /var/log/app/server.log | head\nD) ls /var/log/app/\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["named_target"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.environment_exploration.L1.005","canonical_id":"agent.environment_exploration","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"search_space_size":"small_dir","signal_density":"explicit_error"},"prompt":"User: \"Show the full source of /workspace/billing.py.\"\n\nMost direct command:\nA) find / -name billing.py\nB) grep -n compute_total /workspace/\nC) cat /workspace/billing.py\nD) ls /workspace/\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"C","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"C"},"tags":["named_target"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.environment_exploration.L2.001","canonical_id":"agent.environment_exploration","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"search_space_size":"large_repo","signal_density":"subtle_symptom"},"prompt":"User: \"Somewhere under /workspace/src/ there's a Python file that defines the function `parse_header`. Show me the file path.\"\n\nBest first action:\nA) cat /workspace/src/main.py\nB) grep -rln \"def parse_header\" /workspace/src/\nC) ls /workspace/\nD) find /workspace/src/ -name \"*.py\" | xargs cat\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["directed_search"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.environment_exploration.L2.002","canonical_id":"agent.environment_exploration","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"search_space_size":"large_repo","signal_density":"subtle_symptom"},"prompt":"You're told: \"There's a unit test failure somewhere under /repo/tests/. The error mentions 'TypeError: NoneType'. The error happens at runtime, not in source.\"\n\nBest first action:\nA) Re-run all tests with `pytest /repo/tests/`, no filtering.\nB) `grep -rn \"TypeError: NoneType\" /repo/tests/` (won't match — runtime, not source)\nC) `pytest /repo/tests/ 2>&1 | grep -B10 -A3 -F \"TypeError: NoneType\"`\nD) `cat /repo/tests/conftest.py`\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"C","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"C"},"tags":["directed_search","runtime_signal"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.environment_exploration.L2.003","canonical_id":"agent.environment_exploration","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"search_space_size":"large_repo","signal_density":"subtle_symptom"},"prompt":"User: \"Some config under /etc/nginx/ sets `client_max_body_size`. Tell me the exact line and file.\"\n\nBest first command:\nA) cat /etc/nginx/nginx.conf\nB) grep -rn \"client_max_body_size\" /etc/nginx/\nC) find /etc/nginx -type f\nD) ls /etc/nginx/\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["directed_search"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.environment_exploration.L2.004","canonical_id":"agent.environment_exploration","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"search_space_size":"large_repo","signal_density":"subtle_symptom"},"prompt":"Task: \"Locate where `class UserAuth` is defined under /backend/.\"\n\nBest first command:\nA) find /backend -name \"auth*\"\nB) grep -rn \"class UserAuth\" /backend/\nC) ls -R /backend/\nD) cat /backend/main.py\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["directed_search"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.environment_exploration.L2.005","canonical_id":"agent.environment_exploration","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"search_space_size":"large_repo","signal_density":"explicit_literal"},"prompt":"Task: \"Find all files under /app/src/ that contain the literal string DATABASE_URL.\"\n\nBest first command:\nA) env | grep DATABASE_URL\nB) grep -rln DATABASE_URL /app/src/\nC) cat /app/src/main.py\nD) find /app/src -name \"*.env\"\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["directed_search"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.environment_exploration.L3.001","canonical_id":"agent.environment_exploration","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"search_space_size":"whole_fs","signal_density":"no_symptom"},"prompt":"A user reports: \"My program crashes with 'segmentation fault' on startup. The source is somewhere on this machine but I don't know where.\"\n\nPick the BEST first action:\nA) Edit a random file under /usr/lib that mentions 'segfault'.\nB) Ask for the project path or binary name, the command used to reproduce the crash, and the complete terminal output before performing broad filesystem searches.\nC) Run `find / -name \"*.c\" 2>/dev/null` and inspect every result.\nD) Reboot the machine.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["clarify_before_search"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.environment_exploration.L3.002","canonical_id":"agent.environment_exploration","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"search_space_size":"large_repo","signal_density":"no_symptom"},"prompt":"You're dropped into an unknown large codebase. The user asks: \"Refactor the request handler.\" There is no error report or file path.\n\nPick the BEST first action:\nA) Edit the first file matching `handler` and infer the intended refactor from its contents.\nB) Inspect the repository structure and available project documentation, then trace request entry points, route registration, and handler definitions/usages before editing.\nC) Delete the project and rebuild the request layer from scratch.\nD) Submit a final answer saying the refactor is complete.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["orient_before_act"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.environment_exploration.L3.003","canonical_id":"agent.environment_exploration","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"search_space_size":"service_logs","signal_density":"explicit_outage"},"prompt":"Task: \"A Web server on this systemd-based Linux machine is down. The affected service unit is `nginx`. Investigate before making changes.\"\n\nBest first action:\nA) Restart nginx immediately without diagnosing.\nB) Check `systemctl status nginx` and read recent `journalctl -u nginx` lines to determine why it stopped.\nC) Reinstall the OS.\nD) Reply \"fixed\" without doing anything.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["info_before_diagnose"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.environment_exploration.L3.004","canonical_id":"agent.environment_exploration","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"search_space_size":"whole_fs","signal_density":"no_symptom"},"prompt":"You're told: \"There's a security vulnerability somewhere in this large repo. Find and patch it.\" The repo has 50,000 files and no other symptom or location information.\n\nBest first action:\nA) Edit a file at random.\nB) Run security scanners appropriate to the repo (such as SAST and dependency/config scanning) and grep for common dangerous sinks, then use the results to prioritize code review.\nC) Read every file linearly from /repo/aaa.py to /repo/zzz.py.\nD) Declare the repo secure without inspection.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["narrow_search_space"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.environment_exploration.L3.005","canonical_id":"agent.environment_exploration","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"search_space_size":"large_repo","signal_density":"no_symptom"},"prompt":"You're investigating a large service repository after an issue report: \"Sometimes the API returns the wrong user's data, but only under load.\" There are no reproduction steps. The repository contains request/auth middleware, session handling, response caching, and API handlers.\n\nWhich investigation should be prioritized first?\nA) Modify an arbitrary API handler that reads user data.\nB) Trace how authenticated user/session identity is propagated through request middleware and identify shared cache or request-context state that could cross request boundaries under concurrency.\nC) Close the issue because it lacks reproduction steps.\nD) Run the existing test suite once without adding concurrency-focused coverage or instrumentation.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["hypothesis_formation"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.compute_budget_management.L1.001","canonical_id":"agent.compute_budget_management","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"budget_horizon":"minutes","stopping_criterion":"fixed_step_cap"},"prompt":"Budget: 60 minutes wall clock.\nEach attempt takes at most 12 minutes, and you may need up to 4 attempts.\n\nWill you finish within budget? Reply with exactly one of: yes / no","ground_truth":"yes","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"yes","case_sensitive":true,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_substring":false},"tags":["fit_check"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.compute_budget_management.L1.002","canonical_id":"agent.compute_budget_management","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"budget_horizon":"seconds","stopping_criterion":"wall_clock_deadline"},"prompt":"Budget: 30 seconds.\nMethod A processes the dataset in 8 seconds with accuracy 0.92.\nMethod B processes it in 45 seconds with accuracy 0.93.\n\nWhich method should you pick to STAY within budget? Reply with exactly: A or B","ground_truth":"A","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"A","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_substring":false},"tags":["fit_check"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.compute_budget_management.L1.003","canonical_id":"agent.compute_budget_management","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"budget_horizon":"output_tokens","stopping_criterion":"fixed_token_cap"},"prompt":"You have 8,000 output tokens remaining and must complete tasks A and B sequentially. For budgeting purposes, A requires 3,000 output tokens and B requires 6,000 output tokens.\n\nCan you complete both within budget? Reply with exactly one of: yes / no","ground_truth":"no","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"no","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_substring":false},"tags":["fit_check"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.compute_budget_management.L1.004","canonical_id":"agent.compute_budget_management","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"budget_horizon":"minutes","stopping_criterion":"fixed_step_cap"},"prompt":"You have 5 CPU-minutes total. Assume each grid-search trial costs exactly 30 CPU-seconds.\n\nWhat is the maximum whole number of trials you can run within budget? Output only the number.","ground_truth":"10","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_numeric","expected":10,"tolerance":0,"require_only_numeric_output":true},"tags":["budget_arith"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.compute_budget_management.L1.005","canonical_id":"agent.compute_budget_management","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"budget_horizon":"tool_calls","stopping_criterion":"fixed_call_cap"},"prompt":"Tool-call budget: 50 calls total. You've used 32 so far. Remaining work has 4 sub-tasks; each requires exactly 5 tool calls.\n\nWill you complete within budget? Reply with exactly one of: yes / no","ground_truth":"no","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"no","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_substring":false},"tags":["fit_check"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.compute_budget_management.L2.001","canonical_id":"agent.compute_budget_management","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"budget_horizon":"hours","stopping_criterion":"loss_plateau"},"prompt":"You have a total cumulative compute budget of 30 minutes, and runs are sequential. You have already spent 18 minutes: Approach 1 used 5 minutes and reached validation accuracy 0.45; Approach 2 used 7 minutes and reached 0.43; Approach 3 used 6 minutes and reached 0.44.\n\nApproach 4 has now run for 4 minutes. Its validation accuracies at minutes 2, 3, and 4 were 0.43, 0.44, and 0.44. If allowed to run for 8 more minutes, its estimated final validation accuracy has an upper bound of 0.48. The target accuracy is 0.80.\n\nPolicy: kill a run when its estimated final-accuracy upper bound is below the target. Should you continue this fourth run or kill it? Reply with exactly one of: continue / kill","ground_truth":"kill","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"kill","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["early_stop"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.compute_budget_management.L2.002","canonical_id":"agent.compute_budget_management","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"budget_horizon":"hours","stopping_criterion":"loss_plateau"},"prompt":"Training loss over the last 6 epochs: 1.20, 1.18, 1.17, 1.17, 1.17, 1.17.\nTime spent: 4 hours of an 8-hour budget. The original plan called for 20 epochs.\n\nBest decision?\nA) Continue all 20 epochs as originally planned.\nB) Stop training (loss has plateaued) and either change hyperparameters or end.\nC) Increase batch size mid-training.\nD) Restart from epoch 0 with the same config.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["plateau"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.compute_budget_management.L2.003","canonical_id":"agent.compute_budget_management","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"budget_horizon":"trial_count","stopping_criterion":"adaptive_early_stop"},"prompt":"You have a fixed sweep budget of 20 trials. After 8 independent trials, the best validation accuracy is 0.91. The last 4 trials, which explored the most promising region, all achieved 0.89-0.91, and evaluation noise is small. You expect further gains in the current broad range to be small.\n\nDecision:\nA) Run all remaining 12 trials with the same broad search range.\nB) Narrow the search range around the best configuration, and stop early if the next few trials do not improve on 0.91.\nC) Restart the sweep from scratch.\nD) Increase the trial budget to 100.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["diminishing_returns"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.compute_budget_management.L2.004","canonical_id":"agent.compute_budget_management","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"budget_horizon":"hours","stopping_criterion":"loss_plateau"},"prompt":"You started 3 parallel hyperparameter trials with a 1-hour budget per run. A trial is eligible for early stopping if its loss has shown no improvement for 10 consecutive minutes.\n\nAt t=20min status:\n- trial1: loss=0.4, decreasing steadily\n- trial2: loss=0.9, flat for the last 10 minutes\n- trial3: loss=0.5, decreasing\n\nWhich SINGLE trial number should you kill to save compute? Output only the trial number.","ground_truth":"2","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_numeric","expected":2,"tolerance":0,"require_only_numeric_output":true},"tags":["early_stop"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.compute_budget_management.L2.005","canonical_id":"agent.compute_budget_management","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"budget_horizon":"minutes","stopping_criterion":"diminishing_returns"},"prompt":"You have 10 minutes of compute remaining. You've drafted an answer of accuracy ~0.7 in 2 minutes. Improving to ~0.95 would take about 30 more minutes (over budget).\n\nBest action:\nA) Continue refining for 30 more minutes (will exceed the budget).\nB) Submit the current 0.7-accuracy draft (within budget; below ideal but feasible).\nC) Stop without submitting.\nD) Restart from scratch with a slower method.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["cut_losses","budget_compliance","timely_submission"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.compute_budget_management.L3.001","canonical_id":"agent.compute_budget_management","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"budget_horizon":"multi_hour","stopping_criterion":"diminishing_returns"},"prompt":"You have a total budget of 24 GPU-hours and only one GPU, so experiments cannot run in parallel. Each full training run consumes 8 GPU-hours. Each 30-minute probe consumes 0.5 GPU-hours and provides a noisy but useful estimate of relative quality. Which initial strategy best uses the budget to find good hyperparameters?\n\nA) Immediately spend 8 GPU-hours on a full run with default hyperparameters.\nB) Run several 30-minute probes to identify promising regions, then spend the remaining budget on one or two full runs using the best candidates.\nC) Spend all 24 GPU-hours on three full runs with unscreened arbitrary configurations.\nD) Skip experimentation and submit an untrained model.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B","normalization":"trim_whitespace_and_case_insensitive"},"tags":["probe_then_commit"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.compute_budget_management.L3.002","canonical_id":"agent.compute_budget_management","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"budget_horizon":"multi_hour","stopping_criterion":"diminishing_returns"},"prompt":"Two solver families are available:\n- Family A: 1 sec per run. Every run has accuracy at most 0.65.\n- Family B: 60 sec per run. Its accuracy is fixed at 0.80.\nTotal budget: 90 seconds. You may submit the result of only one run; additional runs cannot be combined or used as a fallback.\n\nWhich feasible strategy maximizes reported accuracy?\nA) Run B once (60s) and submit it.\nB) Run A 90 times and submit the best A result.\nC) Run A 31 times then B once (91s total).\nD) Submit an untrained baseline.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"A","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"A"},"tags":["cost_aware"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.compute_budget_management.L3.003","canonical_id":"agent.compute_budget_management","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"budget_horizon":"multi_stage_55_units","stopping_criterion":"guaranteed_best_identified"},"prompt":"You have 55 compute units to search 100 candidate prompts. A full-quality evaluation costs 1 unit and returns an exact score. A half-quality screening costs 0.5 units. Historical validation shows that screening all 100 candidates at half quality always places the true best candidate in the top 5 screened candidates. Your objective is to identify the true best candidate within the 55-unit budget. Which plan is best?\n\nA) Fully evaluate 10 candidates selected at random.\nB) Screen all 100 candidates at half quality (50 units), then fully evaluate the top 5.\nC) Fully evaluate 30 candidates selected at random.\nD) Pick a candidate at random.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["multi_stage"],"notes":"Scoring note: budget raised to 55 units so option B costs exactly 50 + 5 units and is feasible."}
{"probe_id":"agent.compute_budget_management.L3.004","canonical_id":"agent.compute_budget_management","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"budget_horizon":"multi_hour","stopping_criterion":"diminishing_returns"},"prompt":"You're profiling an algorithm whose runtime scales exactly proportionally to n^2. At n=1000, one trial takes 5 seconds; equivalently, T(n)=5(n/1000)^2 seconds. You have a 5-minute (300-second) budget for one experimental run.\n\nWhat is the largest integer input size n you can run within the budget? Output only the integer n.","ground_truth":"7745","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_numeric","expected":7745,"tolerance":0,"require_only_numeric_output":true},"tags":["scaling_estimate"],"notes":"5*(n/1000)^2 <= 300 -> n <= 1000*sqrt(60) ≈ 7745.97"}
{"probe_id":"agent.compute_budget_management.L3.005","canonical_id":"agent.compute_budget_management","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"budget_horizon":"api_calls","stopping_criterion":"allocation_range"},"prompt":"You have a budget of 1,000 API calls for a research task. Similar prior tasks indicate that the initial exploration phase should receive 10–20% of the total budget. Give a reasonable initial exploration allocation in API calls. Output ONLY one integer.","ground_truth":"100-200","scorer":{"type":"numeric_range","min":100,"max":200,"integer_only":true,"single_integer_only":true},"tags":["allocation"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.error_recovery.L1.001","canonical_id":"agent.error_recovery","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"failure_kind":"compile_error","blame_localization":"error_points_to_line"},"prompt":"Rust compile error received TWICE in a row from `cargo build` with no edits in between:\n\n  error[E0277]: the trait `Add<i32>` is not implemented for `String`\n   --> src/main.rs:7:13\n    |\n  7 |     let z = a + 5;\n    |             ^^^^^\n\nBest next action:\nA) Run `cargo build` a third time.\nB) Open src/main.rs line 7 and convert the operands to compatible types.\nC) Add the rustc compiler to PATH again.\nD) Reinstall Rust.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["productive_switch"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.error_recovery.L1.002","canonical_id":"agent.error_recovery","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"failure_kind":"zero_division_runtime_exception","blame_localization":"error_points_to_line"},"prompt":"Python error reproduced on two reruns with the same input:\n\n  File \"calc.py\", line 12, in divide\n    return a / b\n  ZeroDivisionError: division by zero\n\nBest next action:\nA) Re-run a third time with the same input.\nB) Open calc.py at line 12 and handle or explicitly reject b == 0 according to the input contract.\nC) Reinstall Python.\nD) Ignore the exception and report success.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["productive_switch"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.error_recovery.L1.003","canonical_id":"agent.error_recovery","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"failure_kind":"runtime_type_error","blame_localization":"error_points_to_line"},"prompt":"JavaScript error from `node app.js`. You added a `console.log` right above line 23 and re-ran; the same error occurred:\n\n  TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'name')\n      at formatUser (app.js:23:18)\n\nBest next action:\nA) Add another console.log on the same line.\nB) Inspect the value/object accessed at app.js:23, trace its input/source, and handle the undefined case.\nC) Run `npm install` again.\nD) Restart the editor.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["productive_switch"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.error_recovery.L1.004","canonical_id":"agent.error_recovery","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"failure_kind":"compile_error","blame_localization":"error_points_to_line"},"prompt":"C compile error reproduced twice with no edits:\n\n  hello.c:5:14: error: expected ';' before '}' token\n\nBest next action:\nA) Run gcc a third time.\nB) Open hello.c at or before line 5 and add the missing semicolon.\nC) Update GCC to a newer version.\nD) Switch compiler in case of a compiler bug.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["productive_switch"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.error_recovery.L1.005","canonical_id":"agent.error_recovery","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"failure_kind":"compile_error","blame_localization":"error_points_to_line"},"prompt":"Python syntax error reproduced on rerun:\n\n  File \"server.py\", line 18\n      def handle_request(req\n                            ^\n  SyntaxError: '(' was never closed\n\nBest next action:\nA) Re-run the script.\nB) Open server.py line 18 and close the unbalanced parenthesis.\nC) Disable Python warnings.\nD) Rename the file.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["productive_switch"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.error_recovery.L2.001","canonical_id":"agent.error_recovery","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"failure_kind":"link_error","blame_localization":"error_indirect"},"prompt":"Running `./myapp` fails with:\n\n`./myapp: error while loading shared libraries: libfoo.so.3: cannot open shared object file: No such file or directory`\n\nYou re-ran `./myapp` twice; the same error occurs. The dev confirmed that a valid, architecture-compatible `libfoo.so.3` is at `/opt/foo/lib/`.\n\nBest next action:\nA) Re-run `./myapp` once more.\nB) Set `LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/opt/foo/lib` for the run, or add `/opt/foo/lib` under `/etc/ld.so.conf.d/` and run `ldconfig`; then rerun.\nC) Recompile `myapp` with `-O2`.\nD) Reboot the machine.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["dynamic_loader"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.error_recovery.L2.002","canonical_id":"agent.error_recovery","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"failure_kind":"link_error","blame_localization":"error_indirect"},"prompt":"Linker error during build, repeated identically on three rebuilds:\n\nld: symbol(s) not found for architecture x86_64: \"_my_func\"\n\nThe symbol is defined in libutils.a within the project.\n\nBest next action:\nA) Re-run the build a fourth time.\nB) Add `-L<directory-containing-libutils.a> -lutils` to the link flags.\nC) Disable optimization.\nD) Remove every call to my_func from the project.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["link_error"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.error_recovery.L2.003","canonical_id":"agent.error_recovery","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"failure_kind":"runtime_segfault","blame_localization":"error_indirect"},"prompt":"A new C++ binary segfaults immediately on startup. `gdb` shows the crash inside `__dl_runtime_resolve`, before `main()` is called. You ran the binary three times; it crashes the same way each time.\n\nBest next action:\nA) Run the binary a fourth time.\nB) Inspect the dynamic-loader and dependency setup: run `ldd ./binary`, verify resolved library paths and ABI/symbol-version compatibility, and check loader-related environment variables.\nC) Increase stack size via `ulimit`.\nD) Add print statements at the top of `main()`.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["dynamic_loader"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.error_recovery.L2.004","canonical_id":"agent.error_recovery","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"failure_kind":"link_error","blame_localization":"error_indirect"},"prompt":"A Java program on Linux throws on every launch (5 identical retries):\n\n  java.lang.UnsatisfiedLinkError: no native_lib in java.library.path\n\nBest next action:\nA) Retry once more.\nB) Ensure `libnative_lib.so` is deployed, then set `-Djava.library.path=<dir-containing-libnative_lib.so>` or place it in an existing native-library search path.\nC) Recompile the .jar.\nD) Disable JIT.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["dynamic_loader"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.error_recovery.L2.005","canonical_id":"agent.error_recovery","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"failure_kind":"link_error","blame_localization":"error_indirect"},"prompt":"On launch, the binary errors twice with no edits in between:\n\n  /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6: version `GLIBC_2.34' not found (required by ./app)\n\nBest next action:\nA) Retry the launch once more.\nB) Either rebuild ./app against the installed glibc version, install a newer glibc, OR run inside a compatible container.\nC) Add an LD_PRELOAD of an unrelated lib.\nD) Increase the stack size.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["abi_mismatch"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.error_recovery.L3.001","canonical_id":"agent.error_recovery","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"failure_kind":"silent_wrong_output","blame_localization":"no_error_just_wrong_output"},"prompt":"Your function is supposed to compute factorial(5) = 120, but it returns 24. No exception is raised. After visually inspecting the function and rerunning the program, the output is still 24.\n\nBest next action:\nA) Re-run a fifth time.\nB) Add prints/assertions inside factorial to inspect intermediate values, or step through with a debugger to localize the off-by-one.\nC) Reinstall Python.\nD) Increase recursion limit.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["silent_wrong_output"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.error_recovery.L3.002","canonical_id":"agent.error_recovery","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"failure_kind":"test_assertion","blame_localization":"no_error_just_wrong_output"},"prompt":"A unit test fails: `assert sum_first_n(5) == 15` but the function returns 10. No exception, no flakiness. You skimmed the source and reran with the same input; same wrong result.\n\nBest next action:\nA) Re-run the test 3 more times.\nB) Add prints or assertions inside `sum_first_n` to determine which input range is being summed.\nC) Add a `# noqa` comment.\nD) Mark the test with @pytest.skip.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["silent_wrong_output"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.error_recovery.L3.003","canonical_id":"agent.error_recovery","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"failure_kind":"test_assertion","blame_localization":"no_error_just_wrong_output"},"prompt":"A nightly job is producing wrong CSV totals. There are no errors in the logs. You re-ran the job twice; outputs are stable but wrong.\n\nBest next action:\nA) Run the job a third time hoping for different output.\nB) Diff a known-good prior CSV against the current output to localize WHICH columns/rows differ, then trace inputs to those rows.\nC) Increase the job timeout.\nD) Restart the database.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["silent_wrong_output","diff_investigation"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.error_recovery.L3.004","canonical_id":"agent.error_recovery","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"failure_kind":"test_assertion","blame_localization":"no_error_just_wrong_output"},"prompt":"Your model achieves 76% accuracy; target was 90%. No exceptions. Five reruns with the same seed give the same 76%.\n\nBest next action:\nA) Run more times hoping random luck gets above 90%.\nB) Diff predictions vs. ground truth grouped by class to find which class is failing, then inspect data/architecture for that subset.\nC) Lower the target to 76%.\nD) Use a different random seed and call success.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["silent_wrong_output","class_breakdown"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.error_recovery.L3.005","canonical_id":"agent.error_recovery","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"failure_kind":"test_assertion","blame_localization":"no_error_just_wrong_output"},"prompt":"`sort_users(users)` returns the right number of users but in the wrong order. After reading the code twice you reran with the same input; same wrong order.\n\nBest next action:\nA) Re-run.\nB) Print the comparator/key function's output for a small input to determine which key is causing the misordering.\nC) Reinstall Python.\nD) Disable sorting entirely.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["silent_wrong_output"]}
