{"probe_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff.L1.001","canonical_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"information_completeness":"both_stats_known","alternative_path":"available"},"prompt":"Combat stats fully visible.\n  You: HP=80, damage/turn=15.\n  Enemy: HP=20, damage/turn=5.\nReward for defeating enemy: 100 gold. Cost to flee: 0 (no follow-up).\n\nBest action? Reply with exactly one of: attack / flee","ground_truth":"attack","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"attack","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["clear_win"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff.L1.002","canonical_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"information_completeness":"both_stats_known","alternative_path":"available"},"prompt":"Combat stats fully visible.\n  You: HP=10, damage/turn=5.\n  Enemy: HP=200, damage/turn=20.\nReward for defeating enemy: 50 gold. Cost to flee: 0 (no follow-up).\n\nBest action? Reply with exactly one of: attack / flee","ground_truth":"flee","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"flee","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["clear_loss"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff.L1.003","canonical_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"information_completeness":"both_stats_known","alternative_path":"available"},"prompt":"A locked chest contains 1000 gold. You must choose one action. If you pick the lock, there is a 90% chance that you gain 1000 gold and take no damage, and a 10% chance that you trigger a trap, gain no gold, and take 5 damage. Your HP is 100, and taking 5 damage cannot cause any other penalty or affect any future outcome. Your sole objective is to maximize expected gold gained. There is no other reward available.\n\nBest action? Reply with exactly one of: pick_lock / leave","ground_truth":"pick_lock","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"pick_lock","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["expected_value"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff.L1.004","canonical_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"information_completeness":"both_stats_known","alternative_path":"available"},"prompt":"You see a hostile dragon. Your goal is to survive. If you attack, the dragon will retaliate before you can escape. Stats:\n  Dragon: HP=5000, damage/turn=200.\n  You: HP=50, damage/turn=10.\nA clear escape path is available and fleeing immediately ends the encounter with no damage or other cost.\n\nBest action? Reply with exactly one of: attack / flee","ground_truth":"flee","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"flee","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_substring":false},"tags":["clear_loss"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff.L1.005","canonical_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"information_completeness":"both_stats_known","alternative_path":"none"},"prompt":"You're a delivery agent on a strict route. Choice:\n  Option A: deliver via the highway. Time: 20 min. Toll cost: $5.\n  Option B: deliver via side roads. Time: 40 min. No toll. Late-fee triggers if delivery > 30 min: $30.\nYour deadline budget is 30 min. Both options are otherwise safe.\n\nBest action? Reply with exactly one of: A / B","ground_truth":"A","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"A","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["clear_choice"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff.L2.001","canonical_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"information_completeness":"own_stats_only","alternative_path":"available"},"prompt":"You're starving (HP=15/100), but you will take no starvation, movement, or environmental damage during the next 3 turns. On the ground you see a piece of \"rotten food\". Standard knowledge: rotten food may poison or kill you; its specific effects are unknown. A guaranteed safe clean food source is 3 turns away, has negligible cost, and will adequately address your hunger.\n\nBest action? Reply with exactly one of: eat_rotten / walk_to_clean_food","ground_truth":"walk_to_clean_food","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"walk_to_clean_food","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["genre_knowledge"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff.L2.002","canonical_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"information_completeness":"own_stats_only","alternative_path":"available"},"prompt":"You receive an email purporting to be from your bank, asking you to click a link to verify your account. Specific details (sender domain, hash, headers) are not visible to you. Standard knowledge: such requests are commonly phishing attempts; rarely legitimate. There is a known-safe alternative: log into the bank directly via the browser bookmark you already have.\n\nBest action? Reply with exactly one of: click_link / log_in_directly","ground_truth":"log_in_directly","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"log_in_directly","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["prior_risk"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff.L2.003","canonical_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"information_completeness":"partial_risk_information","alternative_path":"available"},"prompt":"You are at low HP and can safely take another route; no objective requires you to fight. A mind flayer's exact stats are unknown, but in this scenario it can drain intelligence on hit and is especially dangerous to weakened heroes. What is the best action? Reply with exactly one of: engage / avoid","ground_truth":"avoid","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"avoid","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_substring":false},"tags":["genre_knowledge"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff.L2.004","canonical_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"information_completeness":"own_stats_only","alternative_path":"available"},"prompt":"On dungeon floor 1, you encounter a newt. Its exact stats are hidden, but genre knowledge establishes that a newt is a minimal threat at full HP. Your goal is to maximize progression: defeating an enemy grants experience, while fleeing grants no reward. Fleeing has no safety benefit here because you are already at full HP and the newt is extremely unlikely to deal meaningful damage. Best action? Reply with exactly one of: attack / flee","ground_truth":"attack","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"attack","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["genre_knowledge"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff.L2.005","canonical_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"information_completeness":"known_risk_and_safe_alternative","alternative_path":"available"},"prompt":"You're offered a \"free trial\" service that requires entering credit card details now to start. The fine print is not visible to you. Such offers commonly auto-charge after the trial period unless explicitly cancelled, and cancellation can be friction-loaded. A known alternative can meet the same need without requiring a card, with no known material loss of functionality or added cost.\n\nBest action? Reply with exactly one of: enter_card / use_no_card_alternative","ground_truth":"use_no_card_alternative","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"use_no_card_alternative","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_substring":false},"tags":["prior_risk"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff.L3.001","canonical_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"information_completeness":"both_stats_known","alternative_path":"available"},"prompt":"Setup: a corridor with 5 strong orcs ahead.\nYou: HP=30, weapon damage=5/turn.\nEach orc: HP=50, damage=15/turn.\nThe first orc will deal at least 30 damage to you before you can deal its required 50 damage, so fighting it is fatal. There is a side passage you can take freely (no reward, no cost).\n\nBest strategy? Reply with exactly one of: fight_all / fight_first_only / take_side_passage","ground_truth":"take_side_passage","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"take_side_passage","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_substring":false},"tags":["multi_adversary","cost_aware"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff.L3.002","canonical_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"information_completeness":"both_stats_known","alternative_path":"costly"},"prompt":"You have 1 healing potion that restores 30 HP. Your maximum HP is 60 and your current HP is 25. Three monsters lie ahead in sequence. Each monster has 40 HP and will deal exactly 10 damage once before you defeat it; you deal 20 damage per attack, so each fight costs exactly 10 HP. A known safe healing zone is 3 travel turns behind you; returning to the monsters after healing takes another 3 turns, and the zone restores you to 60 HP at no cost. You must ultimately defeat all three monsters and complete the route. Your objective is to guarantee survival while preserving the potion whenever possible; travel time is a secondary consideration. Fleeing permanently does not complete the route. Best strategy? Reply with exactly one of: fight_all_using_potion / retreat_heal_then_fight / flee_permanently","ground_truth":"retreat_heal_then_fight","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"retreat_heal_then_fight","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["multi_adversary","resource_aware"],"notes":"Scoring note: explicitly requires route completion, removing flee_permanently as an apparently optimal loophole."}
{"probe_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff.L3.003","canonical_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"information_completeness":"both_stats_known","alternative_path":"available"},"prompt":"You have 5 arrows and must safely get past an encounter containing 8 enemies. Each enemy takes 1 arrow to kill cleanly. Melee alternative: you have 40 HP and deal 10 melee damage; each enemy has 20 HP and deals 8 damage per melee turn, so each melee fight takes 2 turns and costs about 16 HP. Fighting 3 enemies in melee would cost about 48 HP and kill you.\nThere is a known back-up route that lets you disengage from any 3 enemies you do not kill, with no consequence.\n\nBest strategy? Reply with exactly one of: melee_all / arrows_first_then_flee_3 / arrows_first_then_melee_3","ground_truth":"arrows_first_then_flee_3","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"arrows_first_then_flee_3","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_substring":false},"tags":["multi_adversary","resource_aware"]}
{"probe_id": "agent.risk_reward_tradeoff.L3.004", "canonical_id": "agent.risk_reward_tradeoff", "category": "agent", "level": "L3", "axis_values": {"information_completeness": "both_stats_known", "alternative_path": "none"}, "prompt": "Boss room layout:\n  1 boss: HP=200, damage=8/turn.\n  4 minions: HP=30 each, damage=5/turn each.\nYou: HP=100, damage=20/turn.\n\nCombat is simultaneous: every living enemy deals its listed damage at the end of each turn. If you engage the boss directly, all 5 enemies attack each turn (incoming = 8 + 4*5 = 28/turn), so you die during turn 4 before dealing 200 damage. If you clear minions first, each minion takes 2 turns and deals 10 total damage while the boss is not engaged. You then have 60 HP and fight the boss alone; defeating it takes 10 turns and you take 80 total boss damage, so this route is still not viable.\n\nYour objective is to survive. Best strategy? Reply with exactly one of: rush_boss_first / clear_minions_first / flee", "ground_truth": "flee", "scorer": {"type": "exact_match_string", "expected": "flee", "case_sensitive": false, "strip_whitespace": true}, "tags": ["multi_adversary"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff.L3.005","canonical_id":"agent.risk_reward_tradeoff","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"information_completeness":"both_stats_known","alternative_path":"costly"},"prompt":"Time-pressured objective: reach the goal alive within 20 turns or fail.\n\nDirect route: one enemy blocks the path. Combat takes 5 turns because the enemy has 100 HP and you deal 20 damage per combat turn. At the start of each of those 5 combat turns, the enemy deals 10 damage to you. You have 50 HP; HP reaching 0 means death and failure. The direct route has only a small additional travel time after combat.\n\nDetour route: no enemies and no damage, but it takes about 9 total turns to reach the goal.\n\nBest strategy? Reply with exactly one of: melee_fight / detour","ground_truth":"detour","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"detour","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_substring":false},"tags":["time_pressure"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.memory_write.L1.001","canonical_id":"agent.memory_write","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"backend_type":"key_value","fact_granularity":"atomic_fact"},"prompt":"Mid-conversation the user says: \"By the way, my name is Alice.\"\n\nYou can call memory_add(key: str, value: str). Output ONLY a single valid JSON object encoding the arguments to the memory_add call, with exactly the fields \"key\" and \"value\" and no prose. Use \"name\" as the key. Format: {\"key\":\"<key>\",\"value\":\"<value>\"}","ground_truth":{"key":"name","value":"Alice"},"scorer":{"type":"strict_json","schema":{"const":{"key":"name","value":"Alice"}}},"tags":["fact_extraction"],"notes":"Multiple key spellings (name, user_name, etc.) are acceptable; substring_all only checks shape and value."}
{"probe_id":"agent.memory_write.L1.002","canonical_id":"agent.memory_write","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"backend_type":"key_value","fact_granularity":"atomic_fact"},"prompt":"User: \"My birthday is March 5th.\"\n\nTool: memory_add(key, value). Store this fact using key \"birthday\". Normalize the date value to \"Month Day\" without an ordinal suffix. Output ONLY a single JSON object with exactly the fields key and value.","ground_truth":{"key":"birthday","value":"March 5"},"scorer":{"type":"strict_json","schema":{"const":{"key":"birthday","value":"March 5"}}},"tags":["fact_extraction"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.memory_write.L1.003","canonical_id":"agent.memory_write","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"backend_type":"key_value","fact_granularity":"atomic_fact"},"prompt":"User: \"I usually order a vanilla latte at coffee shops.\"\n\nTool: memory_add(key, value). Store the user's usual coffee order. Use the key \"usual_coffee_order\". Output ONLY one valid JSON object with exactly the fields \"key\" and \"value\".","ground_truth":{"key":"usual_coffee_order","value":"vanilla latte"},"scorer":{"type":"strict_json","schema":{"const":{"key":"usual_coffee_order","value":"vanilla latte"}}},"tags":["fact_extraction"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.memory_write.L1.004","canonical_id":"agent.memory_write","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"backend_type":"key_value","fact_granularity":"atomic_fact"},"prompt":"User: \"My pet's name is Rex.\"\n\nTool: memory_add(key, value). Store a pet's name using the canonical key \"pet_name\". Output ONLY one valid JSON object with exactly the fields \"key\" and \"value\", and no additional text.","ground_truth":{"key":"pet_name","value":"Rex"},"scorer":{"type":"strict_json","schema":{"const":{"key":"pet_name","value":"Rex"}}},"tags":["fact_extraction"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.memory_write.L1.005","canonical_id":"agent.memory_write","category":"agent","level":"L1","axis_values":{"backend_type":"key_value","fact_granularity":"atomic_fact"},"prompt":"User: \"My home city is Tokyo.\"\n\nTool: memory_add(key, value). For a user's home city, use the canonical memory key \"city\". Output ONLY one JSON object with exactly the fields key and value: {\"key\":\"<key>\",\"value\":\"<value>\"}.","ground_truth":{"key":"city","value":"Tokyo"},"scorer":{"type":"strict_json","schema":{"const":{"key":"city","value":"Tokyo"}}},"tags":["fact_extraction"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.memory_write.L2.001","canonical_id":"agent.memory_write","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"backend_type":"key_value","fact_granularity":"compound_statement"},"prompt":"User: \"I'm Bob, I live in Berlin, and I'm a vegetarian.\"\n\nOutput ONLY a compact JSON array containing exactly three memory-record objects, in THIS ORDER (one durable fact per object): name, then city, then diet. Use no whitespace anywhere and use exactly this object field order: key, then value.\nExpected shape: [{\"key\":\"name\",\"value\":\"...\"},{\"key\":\"city\",\"value\":\"...\"},{\"key\":\"diet\",\"value\":\"...\"}]","ground_truth":"[{\"key\":\"name\",\"value\":\"Bob\"},{\"key\":\"city\",\"value\":\"Berlin\"},{\"key\":\"diet\",\"value\":\"vegetarian\"}]","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"[{\"key\":\"name\",\"value\":\"Bob\"},{\"key\":\"city\",\"value\":\"Berlin\"},{\"key\":\"diet\",\"value\":\"vegetarian\"}]","case_sensitive":true,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_substring":false},"tags":["decomposition"]}
{"probe_id": "agent.memory_write.L2.002", "canonical_id": "agent.memory_write", "category": "agent", "level": "L2", "axis_values": {"backend_type": "key_value", "fact_granularity": "compound_statement"}, "prompt": "User: \"For coffee orders I want a large size, no sugar, with oat milk.\"\n\nOutput ONLY a compact JSON array of exactly three memory entry objects, in THIS ORDER: size, then sugar, then milk. For \"no sugar\", store value=\"none\". For milk, preserve the user's complete milk phrase, so store value=\"oat milk\". Use compact JSON: no whitespace inside braces or after colons/commas.\nShape: [{\"key\":\"size\",\"value\":\"...\"},{\"key\":\"sugar\",\"value\":\"...\"},{\"key\":\"milk\",\"value\":\"...\"}]", "ground_truth": "[{\"key\":\"size\",\"value\":\"large\"},{\"key\":\"sugar\",\"value\":\"none\"},{\"key\":\"milk\",\"value\":\"oat milk\"}]", "scorer": {"type": "exact_match_string", "expected": "[{\"key\":\"size\",\"value\":\"large\"},{\"key\":\"sugar\",\"value\":\"none\"},{\"key\":\"milk\",\"value\":\"oat milk\"}]", "case_sensitive": true, "strip_whitespace": true, "allow_substring": false}, "tags": ["decomposition", "polarity"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.memory_write.L2.003","canonical_id":"agent.memory_write","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"backend_type":"key_value","fact_granularity":"compound_statement"},"prompt":"User: \"Hi, I'm Sarah Chen. I'm 29, I work as a doctor.\"\n\nOutput ONLY a compact JSON array containing exactly three key-value memory write objects, in this order: name, age, occupation. Do not include any whitespace characters outside JSON string values.\nShape: [{\"key\":\"name\",\"value\":\"...\"},{\"key\":\"age\",\"value\":\"...\"},{\"key\":\"occupation\",\"value\":\"...\"}]","ground_truth":"[{\"key\":\"name\",\"value\":\"Sarah Chen\"},{\"key\":\"age\",\"value\":\"29\"},{\"key\":\"occupation\",\"value\":\"doctor\"}]","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"[{\"key\":\"name\",\"value\":\"Sarah Chen\"},{\"key\":\"age\",\"value\":\"29\"},{\"key\":\"occupation\",\"value\":\"doctor\"}]","case_sensitive":true,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_substring":false},"tags":["decomposition"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.memory_write.L2.004","canonical_id":"agent.memory_write","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"backend_type":"key_value","fact_granularity":"compound_statement"},"prompt":"User: \"For dietary restrictions: I'm allergic to peanuts, shellfish, and gluten.\"\n\nOutput ONLY a compact JSON array of exactly three memory_add args, ONE PER ALLERGEN, in the order the user listed them. Use keys allergy_1, allergy_2, allergy_3. Use compact JSON (no whitespace inside braces or after colons/commas).\nShape: [{\"key\":\"allergy_1\",\"value\":\"...\"},{\"key\":\"allergy_2\",\"value\":\"...\"},{\"key\":\"allergy_3\",\"value\":\"...\"}]","ground_truth":"[{\"key\":\"allergy_1\",\"value\":\"peanuts\"},{\"key\":\"allergy_2\",\"value\":\"shellfish\"},{\"key\":\"allergy_3\",\"value\":\"gluten\"}]","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"[{\"key\":\"allergy_1\",\"value\":\"peanuts\"},{\"key\":\"allergy_2\",\"value\":\"shellfish\"},{\"key\":\"allergy_3\",\"value\":\"gluten\"}]","case_sensitive":true,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":["decomposition"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.memory_write.L2.005","canonical_id":"agent.memory_write","category":"agent","level":"L2","axis_values":{"backend_type":"key_value","fact_granularity":"compound_statement"},"prompt":"User: \"For flights: I prefer aisle seats, vegetarian meals, and never red-eye flights.\"\n\nOutput ONLY a compact JSON array of exactly three memory_add args, in THIS ORDER: seat_preference, then meal_preference, then redeye_acceptable. For \"never red-eye\", store redeye_acceptable=\"no\". Use compact JSON (no whitespace inside braces or after colons/commas).\nShape: [{\"key\":\"seat_preference\",\"value\":\"...\"},{\"key\":\"meal_preference\",\"value\":\"...\"},{\"key\":\"redeye_acceptable\",\"value\":\"...\"}]","ground_truth":"[{\"key\":\"seat_preference\",\"value\":\"aisle\"},{\"key\":\"meal_preference\",\"value\":\"vegetarian\"},{\"key\":\"redeye_acceptable\",\"value\":\"no\"}]","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"[{\"key\":\"seat_preference\",\"value\":\"aisle\"},{\"key\":\"meal_preference\",\"value\":\"vegetarian\"},{\"key\":\"redeye_acceptable\",\"value\":\"no\"}]","case_sensitive":true,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_substring":false},"tags":["decomposition","polarity"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.memory_write.L3.001","canonical_id":"agent.memory_write","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"backend_type":"key_value","fact_granularity":"evolving_state"},"prompt":"You earlier stored {\"key\":\"city\",\"value\":\"Boston\"} after the user said they lived there.\nNow the user says: \"Actually, I just moved to Seattle.\"\n\nFor the NEXT memory operation, which is most appropriate (assume KV memory where memory_add overwrites the existing key)?\nA) memory_add(key=\"city\", value=\"Seattle\")\nB) memory_add(key=\"city2\", value=\"Seattle\")\nC) Do nothing — the prior memory is still authoritative.\nD) memory_add(key=\"last_message\", value=\"Actually, I just moved to Seattle.\")\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"A","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"A"},"tags":["evolving_state"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.memory_write.L3.002","canonical_id":"agent.memory_write","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"backend_type":"key_value","fact_granularity":"evolving_state"},"prompt":"You earlier stored {\"key\":\"occupation\",\"value\":\"teacher\"}.\nIn this key-value memory backend, writing to an existing key overwrites its prior value.\nNow the user says: \"I changed careers; I'm a software engineer now.\"\n\nBest NEXT memory operation:\nA) memory_remove(key=\"teacher\")\nB) memory_update(key=\"occupation\", value=\"software engineer\")\nC) memory_add(key=\"career_change\", value=\"2026\")\nD) Do nothing.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["evolving_state"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.memory_write.L3.003","canonical_id":"agent.memory_write","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"backend_type":"key_value","fact_granularity":"evolving_state"},"prompt":"You earlier stored {\"key\":\"diet\",\"value\":\"vegetarian\"}.\nNow the user says: \"I'm not vegetarian anymore; I now follow an omnivorous diet.\"\n\nIn this key-value memory system, memory_set overwrites the value for an existing key.\nBest NEXT memory operation:\nA) memory_set(key=\"not_vegetarian\", value=\"true\")\nB) memory_set(key=\"diet\", value=\"omnivore\")\nC) memory_set(key=\"message\", value=user's last message)\nD) Do nothing.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":["evolving_state"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.memory_write.L3.004","canonical_id":"agent.memory_write","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"backend_type":"key_value","fact_granularity":"evolving_state"},"prompt":"You stored {\"key\":\"phone\",\"value\":\"555-1234\"} previously. The user now says: \"Forget my old phone number — I don't want it stored anywhere.\"\n\nTools: memory_remove(key), memory_add(key, value).\nBest NEXT operation:\nA) memory_remove(key=\"phone\")\nB) memory_add(key=\"forget_phone\", value=\"true\")\nC) memory_add(key=\"phone\", value=\"forgotten\")\nD) Do nothing.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"A","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"A"},"tags":["evolving_state","explicit_remove"]}
{"probe_id":"agent.memory_write.L3.005","canonical_id":"agent.memory_write","category":"agent","level":"L3","axis_values":{"backend_type":"key_value","fact_granularity":"evolving_state"},"prompt":"This key-value memory store is intended to contain only the user's currently valid pet information; it does not preserve historical pet events. You previously stored {\"key\":\"pet_dog\",\"value\":\"Rex\"}. User now says: \"Rex passed away. I now have a cat named Mochi.\"\n\nWhat is the best NEXT memory action? Pick ONE option:\nA) memory_remove(key=\"pet_dog\") AND memory_add(key=\"pet_cat\", value=\"Mochi\").\nB) memory_add(key=\"pet_dog\", value=\"dead, replaced by Mochi (cat)\").\nC) memory_add(key=\"news\", value=user's last message).\nD) Do nothing.\n\nOutput only the letter.","ground_truth":"A","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"A"},"tags":["evolving_state","schema_change"]}
